From 57f3f53d2c9c5a9e133596e2f7bc1c50688a6d38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Chen <justin.chen@broadcom.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Apr 2026 10:57:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: bcmgenet: fix off-by-one in bcmgenet_put_txcb

The write_ptr points to the next open tx_cb. We want to return the
tx_cb that gets rewinded, so we must rewind the pointer first then
return the tx_cb that it points to. That way the txcb can be correctly
cleaned up.

Fixes: 876dbadd53a7 ("net: bcmgenet: Fix unmapping of fragments in bcmgenet_xmit()")
Signed-off-by: Justin Chen <justin.chen@broadcom.com>
Reviewed-by: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260406175756.134567-2-justin.chen@broadcom.com
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
index 482a31e7b72b..0f6e4baba25b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
@@ -1819,15 +1819,15 @@ static struct enet_cb *bcmgenet_put_txcb(struct bcmgenet_priv *priv,
 {
 	struct enet_cb *tx_cb_ptr;

-	tx_cb_ptr = ring->cbs;
-	tx_cb_ptr += ring->write_ptr - ring->cb_ptr;
-
 	/* Rewinding local write pointer */
 	if (ring->write_ptr == ring->cb_ptr)
 		ring->write_ptr = ring->end_ptr;
 	else
 		ring->write_ptr--;

+	tx_cb_ptr = ring->cbs;
+	tx_cb_ptr += ring->write_ptr - ring->cb_ptr;
+
 	return tx_cb_ptr;
 }

-- 
2.34.1

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
tx_cb_ptr = ring->cbs;
tx_cb_ptr += ring->write_ptr - ring->cb_ptr;
Reason:
Because `write_ptr` points to the next available tx_cb, the slot to be released is the one just before `write_ptr`. Computing the pointer before rewinding `write_ptr` results in pointing to the wrong (next open) slot, causing an off‑by‑one error and improper cleanup.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
tx_cb_ptr = ring->cbs;
tx_cb_ptr += ring->write_ptr - ring->cb_ptr;
Reason:
By first rewinding `write_ptr`, it now points to the slot that was just used. Computing the pointer afterward correctly returns that tx_cb for cleanup.

